 "sentences": [
  {
   "text": "This fish swims using human heart cells.",
   "start": 0.02,
   "end": 2.518
  },
  {
   "text": "But it doesn't actually have a heart.",
   "start": 2.94,
   "end": 4.453
  },
  {
   "text": "You see, scientists grew living heart muscle on both sides of an artificial fish's tail.",
   "start": 4.86,
   "end": 9.31
  },
  {
   "text": "When one side contracts, it pulls on the other, triggering that side to contract.",
   "start": 9.82,
   "end": 13.596
  },
  {
   "text": "And this happens over and over again, propelling the fish through the water.",
   "start": 14.1,
   "end": 17.589
  },
  {
   "text": "It doesn't even need a motor.",
   "start": 18.06,
   "end": 19.116
  },
  {
   "text": "And as the cells matured, the fish actually got faster.",
   "start": 19.66,
   "end": 22.56
  },
  {
   "text": "But the scientists weren't trying to build a fish.",
   "start": 23.12,
   "end": 25.472
  },
  {
   "text": "They were figuring out how to build a human heart.",
   "start": 25.94,
   "end": 28.466
  }
 ]
